 the reason, or remove the key.\n\n### IN-02: Rationale constants live only in prose, still open\n\n**File:** `probe/budget.py:3-5`, `tests/test_budget.py:5`\n**Issue:** The 90 s failover and 240 s pager figures exist only in a comment, so nothing fails if either one changes. `OFFERED_BUDGETS` duplicates 30/120/300 as well.\n**Fix:** Optional. Name the figures as constants and test `failover < budget < pager`. This also resolves WR-04.\n\n### IN-03: Tautological and redundant deadline tests\n\n**File:** `tests/test_budget_deadline.py:19-28`, `tests/test_budget.py:10`\n**Issue:**\n- `test_deadline_shifts_one_for_one_with_the_start` is an identity for any `f(x) = x + c`: it holds for `c = 9999`. It catches only a constant-return mutant, which `test_deadline_depends_on_the_start_it_is_given` already catches.\n- `assertIsInstance(..., int)` also accepts `True`. The membership check happens to catch that.\n- Only the mock test checks something unique, namely that the constant is read at call time.\n**Fix:** Drop or replace the shift test with an absolute check such as `deadline_after(0.0) == 120.0`. Keep the mock test.\n\n### IN-04: `ruff check` fails (RUF007)\n\n**File:** `tests/test_budget_deadline.py:24`\n**Issue:** `ruff check` (0.17.1) exits 1 on `zip(START_VALUES, START_VALUES[1:])`, and the project style rules require ruff to pass before committing. There is no ruff config file, so the rule comes from ruff's defaults on this host.\n**Fix:** `import itertools` and use `itertools.pairwise(START_VALUES)`, or drop the test per IN-03.\n\n### IN-05: Earlier review and verification overstate the untracked-state problem\n\n**File:** `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VERIFICATION.md:108`, `01-REVIEW-DISPOSITION.md` (WR-03 row)\n**Issue:** Both files say `.planning/milestone.lock` is untracked and `.gsd/` is not ignored. Neither is true of the current tree; see WR-03. The lock may have been a transient file present at review time.\n**Fix:** Note in the disposition that WR-03 is narrowed to `.planning/state.json` only.\n\n### IN-06: `STATE.md` metadata is stale, and \"complete\" means local-only\n\n**File:** `.planning/STATE.md:5,7,39`; `.planning/state.json` (untracked)\n**Issue:**\n- `state_head: e8e1b13...` lags HEAD (`b7516c2`) by two commits.\n- \"Milestone complete — all phases finished\" is true of local execution, but the branch has not been pushed, PR'd or merged (`git ls-remote origin` shows only `main` and `integration`).\n- `state.json` has `phases: []`, so it carries no record of phase 01.\n- None of these is a false claim of a merge, tag or deletion.\n**Fix:** Let GSD refresh `state_head` on the next state write. Read \"complete\" as pre-ship until `/gsd-ship` lands.\n\n### IN-07: `base_branch` differs between DevFlow and GSD (intentional), and the PR will carry DevFlow config to `main`\n\n**File:** `devflow.toml:1`, `.planning/config.json` (`git.base_branch`)\n**Issue:**\n- `devflow.toml` targets `integration`, while the GSD config targets `main`.\n- This is by design. DevFlow merges phases into `integration` locally, and the Ship stage targets the PR at `main`.\n- Consequence: the PR to `main` includes commit 2814f2c, which adds `devflow.toml` with `base_branch = \"integration\"` and `capture_retention = 64`.\n- `01-01-SUMMARY.md:12` also commits agent token telemetry (`tokens: 115`). It is not sensitive, but it is tool metadata in history.\n**Fix:** None required. Document the two-branch model in `PROJECT.md` so a later reader does not \"fix\" the mismatch.\n\n---\n\n_Reviewed: 2026-10-20_\n_Reviewer: Claude (merged multi-angle review: doc-accuracy, security/leaked-data, CI/build, external-state, generalist deep pass; every finding re-verified against the tree before inclusion)_\n_Depth: deep_\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ---"," phase: 01-retry-budget"," reviewed: 2026-10-20T00:00:00Z","-depth: standard","+depth: deep"," files_reviewed: 6"," files_reviewed_lis